content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 85 °C by handheld IR. The applicable HF-300 limits are housing-surface limits: normal up to 70 °C, alarm at 80 °C and trip at 90 °C. The reading is therefore 15 °C above the normal maximum, 5 °C above the alarm limit and 5 °C below trip: it is an above-alarm condition, not a trip-condition reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Because the bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 °C alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift; this work order is therefore P1.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration is 2.5 mm/s. Figure 3's applicable scale is vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. Numerically, 2.5 is below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/Zone B boundary and falls in Zone A (0.0–2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), not Zone C restricted operation or Zone D damage-likely/stop operation. Formal classification still requires confirmation that the report uses the same RMS measurement basis and represents the highest reading from both housings.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On the reported values, no supplied evidence requires an immediate stop: temperature is below the 90 °C trip value, and the reported vibration is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. SSP-07's immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule applies if vibration is in that highest zone; the above-alarm temperature separately requires the P1 response.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No shaft-seal leakage and no noise are reported, and no numerical leakage or noise acceptance limits are supplied. The leakage troubleshooting row is not triggered by the reported symptom, while absence of noise does not establish that the bearings are unworn; high-temperature troubleshooting and the high-temperature bearing-replacement rule still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — a manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Check grease quantity; the report does not confirm this cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear — a manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Inspect the bearings; the lack of reported noise and Zone A reported vibration do not by themselves confirm or exclude wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment — a manual-listed probable cause of high bearing temperature. Check alignment and correct it to the manual tolerances after applicable work.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Respond within the current shift as P1. Before disassembly, verify and record the drive-end bearing housing surface temperature and confirm the vibration measurement basis and location; retain the 80 °C alarm, 90 °C trip and Figure 3 zone limits for reassessment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If the highest reading is in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any work inside the pump, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and drain and vent before obtaining the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly must be removed, plan its lift as a 68 kg assembly. Use the required lifting equipment, certified lifting equipment and a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor; the HF-300 design permits removal of the rotating assembly without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Investigate and record the high-temperature causes: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings for wear and check shaft alignment. Correct over-greasing or misalignment findings rather than treating bearing replacement alone as a confirmed root-cause repair.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply section 5.3's high-temperature criterion and replace both bearings as a pair, not only the drive-end bearing: install one HF3-512 drive-end bearing 6312-C3 and one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Housing-surface temperature is the manual's documented bearing-temperature measurement method, and the reported temperature is above alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit one new HF3-120 casing gasket; the manual requires this gasket to be replaced whenever the casing is opened. Do not apply seal-specific strip-down steps or torques to the bearing job without an approved bearing procedure.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment to a maximum parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular tolerance of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Return the pump to the documented weekly condition-monitoring regime: measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings and classify the highest value using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing under the high-temperature pair-replacement rule.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing under the high-temperature pair-replacement rule.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional on the casing being opened, because it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 applies to this pump. For any work inside the pump or on its seal, provide electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves before internal pump or seal work.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Obtain a line-break permit for internal pump or seal work, draining and venting first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For any lift of the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, the 25 kg lifting threshold is exceeded: use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment; the manual also expressly requires lifting equipment for this assembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If subsequent measurement places the highest housing vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-109's service is confirmed to be chemically dosed, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The supplied dosing statement identifies P-101 to P-106 on the sodium-hypochlorite-dosed filtered-water line, but does not establish P-109's dosing status.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician, applicable after work that moves the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part-number conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B instead. P-109 is serial HF3-23500, so the bulletin applies to this asset. If seal replacement is added to the scope, use HF3-450B and do not fit HF3-450; the bulletin decision does not itself create a seal-replacement requirement for this no-leakage report.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal installation conflict: manual section 5.2 refers fastener tightening to Table 5, which is not supplied, whereas the applicable bulletin specifies a 30 Nm seal gland nut torque for HF3-450B, states that this was 25 Nm, and says the pre-set cartridge needs no sleeve measurement. For this serial, those bulletin instructions govern an HF3-450B installation; the 30 Nm value is specific to its seal gland nut, not a general pump fastener torque. If that seal work is added, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 2.5 mm/s value an RMS vibration-velocity reading on a bearing housing, and what are the separate drive-end and non-drive-end readings? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified, so the single report value cannot establish that requirement was met (C06, C07).",
    "Which of over-greasing, bearing wear or misalignment is the actual cause? The evidence lists these possibilities but provides no inspection findings or basis for ranking their likelihood (C09).",
    "What grease type, specified quantity and acceptance criterion should the technician use? The troubleshooting table requires a grease-quantity check but the supplied evidence provides none of these details (C09).",
    "Will the bearing repair open the casing or disturb the mechanical seal? This determines whether the conditional casing gasket is required and whether the bulletin-controlled seal parts, installation instructions and additional seal labour must be added (C05, C10, C12, C13).",
    "What approved bearing-specific strip-down/reassembly procedure and general fastener torques apply? Section 5.3 supplies only the pair-replacement rule; section 5.2 is seal-specific, Table 5 is not supplied, and the bulletin's 30 Nm applies only to the HF3-450B seal gland nut (C10, C13).",
    "Is P-109 on a chemically dosed line, and what is the line fluid? SSP-07 makes goggles and nitrile gloves conditional on chemical dosing, while the only asset-specific dosing evidence covers P-101 to P-106 (C15, C16).",
    "What additional labour is required for reading verification, grease inspection and any scope growth? The labour table supplies standards only for seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment, and no seal-replacement allowance is included in the present scope (C12)."
  ]
}
